  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The following table shows the number of days it rained in Madrid during $2019.$\n\n| Rainy days | No-rain days |\n| --- | --- |\n| $63$ | $302$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest ten, determine the approximate ratio of the number of days it rained in Madrid to the number of days it did not rain.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of days that it rained and did not rain by rounding to the nearest $10$:\n\n- Rainy days: $63⟶60$\n\n- No-rain days: $302⟶300$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of days that it rained to the number of days that it did not rain is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{60}{300}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{60÷10}{300÷10}=\\frac{6}{30}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6÷6}{30÷6}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nHence, the ratio of the number of days that it rained and did not rain is approximately $1:5.$",
